# NAME: Cinnado B6 (T23ZN, OS02G10, TM18NA LTE)
# FRAG: soc-xburst1 core ssl
#
# SoC:     Ingenic T23ZN, XBurst1 MIPS32 R1, 64MB RAM (46M+18M split)
# Sensor:  OmniVision OS02G10, 1/2.9" 2MP, I2C 0x3c, reg_addr_size=0 (ZRT bank-switch)
# Cellular: TUGE Technologies TM18NA (UNISOC V8850 baseband), USB (T23 dwc2 host mode)
# MCU:     MindMotion MM32F0020B1T (Cortex-M0), I2C addr 0x11, PIR/battery/power/watchdog
# Flash:   16MB NOR SPI
#
# NOTES:
#  - This is the LTE sibling of cinnado_b6_t23zn_os02g10_atbm6461 (same
#    "Cinnado B6" chassis/PTZ family, T23ZN + OS02G10), but with a TM18NA LTE
#    module in place of the ATBM6461 WiFi/SDIO chip. Reverse-engineered from
#    stock firmware firmware_T23ZN_20260803_2026.bin -- no live hardware access
#    yet, so PTZ/GPIO map below is carried over from the WiFi sibling's own
#    "best available guess... verify on hardware" starting point, not confirmed
#    for this exact variant.
#  - CRITICAL: the stock firmware disables the MCU's hardware watchdog very
#    early in boot (before its normal init sequence) via a dedicated recovery
#    tool. See package/thingino-mcu-wdt, which ships that same extracted vendor
#    binary and runs it from an F00a-prefixed script -- before F00ledd, ahead
#    of the rest of rcF/rcS. If first boot reboot-loops, this is the first
#    thing to suspect (watchdog window tighter than an F-script can catch).
#  - MCU I2C bus CONFIRMED via live hardware + vendor kernel binary analysis:
#    it's GPIO-bitbanged (CONFIG_SOFT_I2C1_GPIO_V12_JZ), SDA=GPIO53/SCL=GPIO52
#    (GPIO_PB(21)/GPIO_PB(20)), not the I2C1_V12_JZ hardware controller. See
#    the kernel fragment and package/all-patches/linux/3.10.14/0092-*.patch.
#  - PTZ motors DISABLED (BR2_THINGINO_MOTORS) for now: the WiFi sibling's
#    copied gpio_tilt map claimed GPIO52/53 for motor ST2/ST3, which directly
#    conflicts with the real MCU I2C pins above -- proof the whole PTZ GPIO
#    map carried over from the sibling is unreliable for this variant, not
#    just those two pins. Needs its own hardware-verification pass before
#    re-enabling.
BR2_INGENIC_SOC_MODEL="t23zn"
BR2_ISP_CLKA_600MHZ=y
BR2_ISP_CLKA_SCLKA=y
BR2_ISP_CLK_200MHZ=y
BR2_ISP_CLK_SCLKA=y
BR2_ISP_PRINT_LEVEL_0=y
BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_CONFIG_FRAGMENT_FILES="$(BR2_EXTERNAL_THINGINO_PATH)/configs/cameras/cinnado_b6_t23zn_os02g10_tm18na/cinnado_b6_t23zn_tm18na.kernel.config"
BR2_PACKAGE_BUSYBOX_SHOW_OTHERS=y
BR2_PACKAGE_I2C_TOOLS=y
BR2_PACKAGE_THINGINO_KOPT_MMC0=y
BR2_PACKAGE_THINGINO_KOPT_MMC0_PB_4BIT=y
BR2_PACKAGE_THINGINO_MCU_WDT=y
BR2_PACKAGE_USBNET=y
BR2_PACKAGE_USBNET_WWAN_SERIAL=y
BR2_SENSOR_1_NAME="os02g10"
BR2_THINGINO_AUDIO=y
BR2_THINGINO_AUDIO_GPIO=63
BR2_THINGINO_RMEM_MB=18
BR2_THINGINO_SDCARD=y
FLASH_SIZE_MB=16
